WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.439
The Waimakariri district is now in a restricted
fire season.

00:00:04.439 --> 00:00:07.879
This means that no fires in the open air can
be lit without a permit

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:10.760
and the season extends until further notice.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:16.519
These restrictions apply to all fires on the
beaches and includes the lighting of fireworks,

00:00:16.519 --> 00:00:19.910
use of outdoor braziers and chimineas.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:24.030
Burning rubbish in drums is also restricted,
unless the drum is fully enclosed

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:25.910
and fitted with a flue.

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:30.520
Charcoal BBQ's are considered fires in the
open and are restricted.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:35.969
However gas BBQ's and pizza ovens fitted with
flues are fine to use.

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:39.409
When applying to the Waimakariri District
Council for a permit,

00:00:39.409 --> 00:00:43.719
it can take up to five days to carry out a site inspection and process  the permit.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:45.120
So apply early.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:50.000
And once you have a permit, any conditions
printed on it, must be observed.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:54.039
Make sure you check out the safety tips in
the video linked below.

00:00:54.039 --> 00:00:57.559
So remember, no open air fires without a permit.

00:00:57.559 --> 00:01:00.779
And as always, think before you light.

